\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::1>
\f1\b\fs48 20. Compact floor-plan-in-words\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::1>
\f2 At the northern end of Sublime Point sits Eloise's visually occluded residence. Her preferred home office and minimal HQ heart operate there, with the compound brig beneath the residence.\
Beyond it are the internal hover pad and auditorium.\
The long squat administrative building contains ordinary Sublime Point offices, including Hayley's. Beneath it lies the station.\
The station connects directly to the 
\f1\b Traverse maglev
\f2\b0  and to the secure service infrastructure leading into Ruined Castle.\
Nearby, still 
\f1\b north of the bushland transition
\f2\b0 , is the concealed vehicle/service entrance into that same underground network.\
Only after this functional zone does the surface road enter bushland and continue towards the residential townhouses.\
Ruined Castle is reached from this northern station/service system.\
It is a largely subterranean installation spreading beneath and into the terrain around Ruined Castle Gully.\
Most of it has no external expression at all.\
Where offices such as Sarah's and Eloise's approach the gully face, they are embedded into the hillside. Minimal windows look into the gully but are obscured by the same class of visual/sensor-confusion technology used by Eloise's residence. From above, the installation remains hillside.\
Within Ruined Castle, laboratories and weapons projects occupy separate secure sectors.\
Kathy's biomedical suite belongs within a segregated medical/biological research sector: deep enough to be highly secure, but more accessible to personnel and logistics than extreme weapons testing.\
Other biological projects occupy separate laboratory suites so a failure in one cannot readily contaminate or destroy the rest.\
Deeper and more isolated again lies the weapons-testing region.\
Project Kebab occupies one of its most secure sectors.\
Its personnel work in secure analysis rooms and operate tests from a remote control room equipped with cameras, sensors, telemetry and potentially absurdly large monitors.\
Beyond that control room, separated by substantial structure and distance, lies the Kebab apparatus chamber.\
That chamber is used by every generation of the Project Kebab machine.\
There is no observation glass.\
Nobody needs to be physically close enough to watch a Gyges disc misbehave ever again.}